model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "A shared app's skill reader must receive, in the Cloud dashboard's server-rendered document, its TypeScript fence colored and its JavaScript fence plain, and the browser must color the JavaScript fence once its engine loads, at desktop and phone width. The browser's highlight engine is held until the blocks are measured, and no block may move by more than half a pixel when the colors arrive. Whether the TypeScript block keeps the server's colors through hydration is not checked while issue #2123 can rebuild it after hydration."
    }
  }
}
